  "strategy": "Our approach takes advantage of the received parent solution (n=95) and refines it using gradient-based optimization. We improve upon the previous strategy by:\n1. Using a variation of SLSQP that handles constraints more effectively\n2. Implementing a multi-resolution optimization where we begin at higher resolutions (2*n) to improve accuracy\n3. Combining coarse and fine optimization phases\n4. Maintaining better repair mechanisms during optimization\n\nApproach and rationale\nThe core idea is to minimize the maximum overlap integral by:\n1. Representing h as a step function on [0,2] space\n2. Using the parent solution as a starting point\n3. Optimizing at multiple resolutions (n, 2n, 3n)\n4. Iteratively improving solutions by:\n   - Repairing constraint violations (integral=1, values in [0,1])\n   - Clipping extreme values\n   - Using gradient-based optimization\n\nThe method is listed below:\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\n\ndef repair_vector(h, n):\n    # First clip to [0,1]\n    h_clip = np.clip(h, 0, 1)\n    sum_clip = np.sum(h_clip)\n    # Required sum is n/2\n    if abs(sum_clip - n/2) < 1e-7:\n        return h_clip\n    # Scale to meet the integral requirement\n    factor = (n/2) / sum_clip if sum_clip != 0 else 1.0\n    h_scaled = h_clip * factor\n    # Clip again in case efficiency lost\n    h_scaled = np.clip(h_scaled, 0, 1)\n    return h_scaled\n\ndef objective_for_n(h_flat, n):\n    # Reshape for the problem\n    h_reshaped = h_flat.reshape(samples)\n    # Compute correlation\n    corr = np.correlate(h_reshaped, 1-h_reshaped, mode='full')\n    # Scale by dx (2/n)\n    max_corr = np.max(corr)\n    return max_corr * (2.0/n)\n\n# Global variables governing the optimization\nsamples = 95  # Parent sample size\ninitial_h_values = global_initial_h_values  # Provided parent solution\n\ndef repair_spatial(vector, length):\n    vector = repair_vector(vector, length)\n    return vector.reshape(length)\n\ndef run(seed=42, budget_s=1100, **kwargs):\n    # Global variables inherited from parent\n    samples_per_method = [95, 190, 380]  # Trying 3 resolutions\n    best_score = float('inf')\n    best_vector = None\n    \n    # Check budget constraints\n    if budget_s < 60:\n        n_list = [95]\n    elif budget_s < 300:\n        n_list = [95, 190]\n    else:\n        n_list = [95, 190, 380]\n    \n    # Initialize time tracking\n    import time\n    start_time = time.time()\n    \n    for n_val in n_list:\n        if n_val == 95:\n            # Use provided initial_h_values\n            initial_vector = initial_h_values.copy()\n        else:\n            # Interpolate parent to obtain new resolution\n            x_old = np.linspace(0, 2, 95)\n            x_new = np.linspace(0, 2, n_val)\n            tck = interpolate.interp1d(x_old, initial_h_values, bounds_error=False, fill_value=0, kind='linear')\n            initial_vector = tck(x_new)\n            # Ensure the interpolated vector is valid\n            initial_vector = repair_vector(initial_vector, n_val)\n            \n        # Setup bounds for minimization\n        bounds = [(0, 1)] * n_val\n        \n        # Optimization - coarse phase\n        res_coarse = minimize(\n            objective_for_n,\n            initial_vector,\n            args=(n_val,),\n            method='L-BFGS-B',\n            bounds=bounds,\n            initial_vector=True,\n            options={'maxiter': 100, 'disp': True}\n        )\n        # Optimization - fine phase\n        res_fine = minimize(\n            objective_for_n,\n            res_coarse.x,\n            args=(n_val,),\n            method='L-BFGS-B',\n            bounds=bounds,\n            options={'maxiter': 200, 'disp': True}\n        )\n        \n        # Repair the fine solution\n        candidate_vector = repair_vector(res_fine.x, n_val)\n        score_val = objective_for_n(candidate_vector, n_val)\n        \n        # Update best solution across resolutions\n        if score_val < best_score:\n            best_score = score_val\n            best_vector = candidate_vector\n        \n        # Check time budget\n        elapsed = time.time() - start_time\n        if elapsed >= budget_s:\n            break\n    \n    n_final = n_val if best_vector is None else len(best_vector)\n    best_vector_initial = best_vector if best_vector is not None else initial_h_values[:n_final]\n    score_val_final = best_score if best_score < float('inf') else objective_for_n(initial_vector, n_final)\n    \n    return (best_vector_initial.astype(np.float64) if best_vector is not None else initial_h_values[:n_final].astype(np.float64)), \\\n           score_val_final, n_final\n```\n\nMathematical specifications\n- Samples: n_val (provides resolution parameter)\n- Objective: min max_{shifts} \u222b h(x)(1-h(x+k)) dx\n- Constraints:\n  - h(x) in [0,1] for all x\n  - \u222b h(x) dx = 1\n\nImplementation procedure\n1. Input: seed, budget_s, and other parameters\n2. Setup:\n   - Determine resolutions to try based on budget\n   - Initialize best score and vector\n3. For each resolution:\n   - If n=95, use provided parent solution\n   - Else, interpolate parent solution to new resolution\n   - Apply coarse optimization phase with L-BFGS-B\n   - Apply fine optimization phase\n   - Repair solution and evaluate score\n   - Update best if improved\n4. Return best solution found\n\nSearch choices and useful variations:\n- We default to 95 points but increase to 190 or 380 points if allowed\n- Optimization uses L-BFGS-B to balance efficiency and robustness\n- Repair mechanism ensures solutions meet integral constraint\n- Time budget is strictly respected\n\nNumerical robustness and memory use:\n- Uses single-threaded minimization\n- Memory proportional to sample size\n- Handles constraint violations via repair mechanism\n\nRuntime safeguards:\n- Time tracking ensures non-exceedance of budget\n- Fallback to parent solution when time runs out\n- Intermediate repairs prevent constraint violations\n\nReturn contract:\n- Returns processed h_values (ending in [0,1] and sum(h)=n/2)\n- Stores score for comparison\n- Records appropriate n\n\nNote: Optimization time increases with sample size. Coarser optimization first provides robustness.",
